    "page": 1,
    "articleTitle": "Small Choices, Better Meals",
    "articleEn": "Eating well is not about giving up the {{food}} you love. A balanced {{diet}} simply means choosing carefully and listening to your {{appetite}} instead of eating out of habit. Once a week I still {{treat}} myself to something rich, and I never feel guilty about it.\n\nMost places now {{cater}} to healthier tastes. Our university makes {{provision}} for students with allergies, and the chefs even decorate plates with {{edible}} flowers. My mother sends me a {{recipe}} every Sunday, so I cook at home rather than order from a {{restaurant}} every night. At school we used to eat in an old {{refectory}}; now the modern {{cafeteria}} offers a salad {{buffet}} where you pay by weight. In summer the staff hold a {{barbecue}} in the garden, and lighter grilled fish replaces heavy meat.\n\nA late {{supper}} is my weakness. I used to finish the day with a huge plate, almost like a {{banquet}}, and then sleep badly. Now I drink a warm {{refreshment}} instead, or take a small {{snack}} such as nuts or yoghurt. When friends visit, I serve a simple {{appetizer}} of raw vegetables and dip before the main course.\n\nTravelling has taught me that healthy {{cuisine}} exists everywhere. The trick is to read the {{menu}} slowly, ask how each dish is cooked, and choose steamed or baked options. Small decisions, repeated every day, matter far more than any strict rule.",
    "articleZh": "吃得健康并不意味着要放弃你喜爱的食物。均衡的饮食只是意味着认真选择,并倾听自己的食欲,而不是出于习惯而进食。每周我还是会款待自己一次,吃点油腻丰盛的东西,而且从不为此感到内疚。\n\n如今大多数地方都开始迎合更健康的口味。我们大学为有过敏症的学生提供特别安排,厨师们甚至用可食用的花朵装饰餐盘。我妈妈每周日都会发给我一个食谱,所以我在家做饭,而不是每天晚上都从餐馆订餐。上学时我们常在一间老旧的食堂里吃饭;现在现代化的自助餐厅提供沙拉自助餐台,按重量付费。夏天,工作人员会在花园里举办烧烤,用口味清淡的烤鱼取代油腻的肉类。\n\n吃夜宵是我的弱点。以前我总是以一大盘食物结束一天,几乎像一场宴会,结果睡得很差。现在我改喝一杯温热的饮品,或者吃一点小零食,比如坚果或酸奶。朋友来访时,我会在主菜之前上一道简单的开胃菜,就是生蔬菜配蘸酱。\n\n旅行让我明白,健康的菜肴到处都有。诀窍是慢慢看菜单,问清楚每道菜是怎么做的,并选择蒸的或烤的做法。每天重复的小决定,远比任何严格的规定更重要。",
