    "id": "c12p5",
    "chapter": 12,
    "page": 5,
    "articleTitle": "Eating Well, Simply",
    "articleEn": "Eating well is simpler than most people think.\n\nStart with fruit. A crisp {{pear}}, a sweet {{plum}} or a juicy {{orange}} costs very little and supplies vitamins your body needs. In summer I keep a cold {{melon}} in the fridge, and I squeeze a {{lemon}} into plain water instead of buying sugary drinks. One {{kiwi}} at breakfast adds fibre as well.\n\nNext, think about what farmers grow. Every {{crop}} in the field ends up on somebody's plate. {{Corn}}, rice and other {{grain}} foods give us steady energy, and {{wheat}} is ground into {{flour}} for bread and noodles. Farmers {{reap}} these harvests in autumn, so prices are often lowest then. On cold mornings I cook oats into {{porridge}}, which is warm, cheap and filling, and I spread a thin layer of sesame {{paste}} on my toast rather than butter.\n\nMeat matters too, but the portion should be modest. {{Livestock}} farms supply {{beef}}, {{pork}} and {{mutton}}, which are rich in iron yet often high in fat. {{Chicken}} and {{turkey}} are leaner, especially without the skin. Nutritionists suggest filling half your plate with vegetables, a quarter with grain, and only a quarter with meat or beans.\n\nNone of this requires expensive supplements. Cook at home, drink water, and choose whole foods more often than packaged ones. Small daily habits, repeated for months, do more for your health than any short diet.",
    "articleZh": "吃得健康,其实比大多数人想的要简单。\n\n先从水果开始。一个脆爽的梨、一颗甜甜的李子,或者一个多汁的橙子,价格都很便宜,却能提供身体需要的维生素。夏天我会在冰箱里放一个凉西瓜;我会把柠檬挤进白水里喝,而不是去买含糖饮料。早餐吃一个奇异果,还能补充纤维。\n\n接下来,想一想农民种的东西。田里的每一种作物最终都会出现在某个人的餐盘上。玉米、大米和其他谷物为我们提供稳定的能量;小麦被磨成面粉,做成面包和面条。农民在秋天收割这些庄稼,所以那时的价格往往最低。天冷的早上,我会把燕麦煮成粥,温热、便宜又管饱;我还会在吐司上涂一层薄薄的芝麻酱,而不用黄油。\n\n肉类也很重要,但分量应该适度。牲畜养殖场提供牛肉、猪肉和羊肉,它们富含铁,但脂肪通常也较高。鸡肉和火鸡肉更瘦一些,尤其是去掉皮之后。营养师建议:餐盘的一半装蔬菜,四分之一装谷物,只留四分之一给肉类或豆类。\n\n这一切都不需要昂贵的保健品。在家做饭,多喝水,并且尽量选择原态食物而不是包装食品。坚持几个月的小小日常习惯,对健康的帮助超过任何短期减肥法。",
