    "id": "c12p8",
    "chapter": 12,
    "page": 8,
    "articleTitle": "Cooking Well, Eating Well",
    "articleEn": "Eating well does not mean eating boring food. In my kitchen I try to {{cook}} meals that are healthy and {{delicious}} at the same time. I rarely {{fry}} anything in deep oil. Instead, I {{bake}} fish in the oven, {{roast}} vegetables until they taste sweet, and {{toast}} one thin {{slice}} of brown bread for breakfast. For a salad, I cut tomatoes, {{squeeze}} half a lemon over them, and {{stir}} in a spoonful of yoghurt to make a light {{sauce}}. It is much better than the {{ketchup}} in the fridge.\n\nFlavour comes from fresh {{ingredients}}, not from salt. I {{grind}} black pepper by hand, and the {{perfume}} of green herbs fills the whole room. A little {{spice}} makes plain rice interesting, although very {{spicy}} dishes upset my stomach. Some vegetables taste {{bitter}} at first, but they help me {{digest}} heavy meals.\n\nI {{soak}} beans overnight so that they cook faster, and I {{dip}} raw carrots into yoghurt for a snack. My students often {{suck}} sweets, {{chew}} sugary {{gum}} all afternoon, and then {{lick}} chocolate off their fingers. That is not real food; it is only sugar. When true {{hunger}} comes, or when I feel {{thirsty}}, I choose fruit and water instead of a pill. No {{supplement}} can replace a {{tasty}}, balanced plate, and a home-cooked dinner is {{yummy}} as well.",
    "articleZh": "吃得健康并不意味着吃得乏味。在我的厨房里，我努力做出既健康又美味的饭菜。我很少用大量的油去炸东西，而是用烤箱烤鱼、把蔬菜烤到发甜，早餐再烤一片薄薄的全麦面包。做沙拉时，我把西红柿切开，挤上半个柠檬的汁，再拌入一勺酸奶，做成清淡的酱汁。这比冰箱里的番茄酱好得多。\n\n味道来自新鲜的food材料，而不是盐。我用手磨黑胡椒，青草药的香气弥漫整个房间。一点香料就能让白米饭变得有滋味，不过太辣的菜会让我的胃不舒服。有些蔬菜一开始吃起来是苦的，但它们能帮我消化油腻的饭菜。\n\n我把豆子泡一整夜，这样煮起来更快；我还会把生胡萝卜蘸酸奶当零食。我的学生常常整个下午都在吮糖果、嚼含糖的口香糖，然后再舔掉手指上的巧克力。那不是真正的食物，那只是糖。当真正的饥饿感来了，或者我感到口渴时，我会选择水果和水，而不是一颗药片。没有任何保健品能取代一盘可口而均衡的饭菜，而且家里做的晚饭同样很好吃。",
