    "id": "c16p8",
    "chapter": 16,
    "page": 8,
    "articleTitle": "Saving a Factory Town",
    "articleEn": "When a factory in our town began to lose money, the owners had to {{choose}} between two paths. Cutting costs quickly would mean a large {{lay-off}}, and nobody wanted to {{fire}} loyal staff. Some managers hoped to {{sack}} only the newest workers, others to {{dismiss}} whole departments or {{discharge}} the night shift. The oldest employees were asked to {{retire}} early, and two junior directors decided to {{resign}} rather than sign the plan.\n\nAn economist was invited to {{recommend}} a better strategy. She argued that the {{failure}} was not the workers' fault but the {{result}} of poor planning: the company had refused to {{change}} its products for ten years. The sudden {{abortion}} of a promising export project had also caused a serious {{loss}}.\n\nHer advice was to {{develop}} greener goods, {{improve}} training, and {{employ}} local graduates instead of expensive consultants. Rather than {{hire}} outsiders, the firm should {{collaborate}} with a nearby college, {{cooperate}} with its suppliers, and {{coordinate}} deliveries to save fuel. Government could help too: officials can {{regulate}} unfair competition and {{sanction}} firms that pollute.\n\nTwo years later, the factory can {{manage}} its debts again, and the town has a real {{opportunity}} to grow in a {{sustainable}} way. Young people finally get a genuine {{chance}} to build careers at home. Money alone cannot {{solve}} such problems, but sensible choices can.",
    "articleZh": "当我们镇上的一家工厂开始亏损时，业主必须在两条路之间做出选择。迅速削减成本意味着大规模裁员，而没有人愿意解雇忠诚的员工。有些管理者希望只开除最新来的工人，另一些人则想撤掉整个部门，或者解散夜班。最年长的员工被要求提前退休，两位年轻的董事决定辞职，而不愿在这份方案上签字。\n\n一位经济学家受邀提出更好的策略建议。她认为，这次失败不是工人的过错，而是规划不善的结果：公司十年来一直拒绝改变自己的产品。一个很有前景的出口项目突然中止，也造成了严重的损失。\n\n她的建议是开发更环保的产品、改进培训，并雇用本地毕业生，而不是聘请昂贵的顾问。与其从外部招人，公司应当与附近的一所学院合作、与供应商协作，并统一协调配送以节省燃料。政府也能帮忙：官员可以监管不公平竞争，并制裁污染企业。\n\n两年后，这家工厂又能够管理好自己的债务，小镇也真正获得了以可持续方式发展的机会。年轻人终于有了在家乡建立职业生涯的真正机遇。仅靠金钱无法解决这样的问题，但明智的选择可以。",
