    "id": "c19p4",
    "chapter": 19,
    "page": 4,
    "articleTitle": "Roles We Play",
    "articleEn": "In our {{neighborhood}}, most people carry several roles at the same time.\n\nLast spring Daniel decided to {{propose}} to Mei in the park where they first met. She said yes, and their {{engagement}} was announced at a family dinner. Three months later they chose to {{marry}} in a small church. The {{wedding}} was simple: forty guests, one cake, and a shy {{kiss}} at the door. For their {{honeymoon}} they took a slow train to the coast.\n\nThen ordinary life began. Daniel is now a {{commuter}} who catches the 7:10 train every morning. At work he is a {{subordinate}} with a demanding {{supervisor}}; the supervisor reports to a department {{manager}}, and the manager reports to the {{boss}} who owns the firm. {{Each}} of them knows their {{respective}} duties, so no {{individual}} has to solve every problem alone.\n\nMei's sister has followed a different path. After five difficult years she decided to {{divorce}}, and the couple agreed to {{separate}} quietly. She is {{single}} again and the {{sole}} carer of her young son. Even so, she is not lonely: she is an active {{member}} of a reading club in the same street, and her neighbours often look after the boy.\n\nRoles change with time. Today you may be someone's employee, tomorrow someone's teacher, partner or parent. What matters is not the title but how carefully we play each part.",
    "articleZh": "在我们的社区里，大多数人同时扮演着好几种角色。\n\n去年春天，丹尼尔决定在他和梅初次相遇的公园里向她求婚。她答应了，他们的订婚消息在一次家庭晚餐上宣布。三个月后，他们选择在一座小教堂里结婚。婚礼很简单：四十位客人、一个蛋糕，还有在门口羞涩的一吻。度蜜月时，他们坐慢车去了海边。\n\n随后，平常的日子开始了。丹尼尔现在是一名通勤者，每天早上赶七点十分的火车。在公司里他是下属，上面有一位要求严格的主管；主管向部门经理汇报，经理再向拥有这家公司的老板汇报。他们每个人都清楚自己各自的职责，所以没有哪一个人需要独自解决所有问题。\n\n梅的姐姐走了另一条路。在艰难的五年之后，她决定离婚，夫妻两人同意平静地分开。她又变成单身，也是年幼儿子唯一的照顾者。即便如此，她并不孤单：她是同一条街上一个读书俱乐部的活跃成员，邻居们也常帮她照看孩子。\n\n角色会随时间改变。今天你可能是某人的员工，明天又是某人的老师、伴侣或父母。重要的不是头衔，而是我们把每个角色扮演得多用心。",
