    "id": "c19p6",
    "chapter": 19,
    "page": 6,
    "articleTitle": "The Roles That Keep a Town Running",
    "articleEn": "Every town needs people to fill its roles. In my neighbourhood, a business {{consultant}} lives next to a {{veterinary}} clinic, where sick animals are treated all day. Across the street, a school {{counselor}} listens to worried teenagers, a British {{solicitor}} prepares legal documents, and an American {{attorney}} advises companies on contracts. On Saturdays, that same quiet lawyer becomes the {{umpire}} at the baseball field. The supermarket {{cashier}} knows everyone's name, the {{fireman}} at the station is a local hero, and the {{nurse}} at the clinic works long night shifts. Our {{gardener}} cuts the grass in the park, and the {{barber}} gives me a cheap {{haircut}} every month. Down by the harbour, a {{fisherman}} sells his catch to the {{butcher}}, who also keeps two horses and pays a boy to {{groom}} them.\n\nLast winter, a robber held a customer {{hostage}} inside the bank. The fireman spoke to him calmly for an hour until the police arrived. Afterwards he said he was not especially brave; he simply did not want to be a {{coward}} in front of his own children.\n\nThese jobs are rarely glamorous. Many people {{toil}} for low pay, and some feel like a {{slave}} to the clock. Outside the station, a {{beggar}} asks passers-by for coins, reminding us that not everyone finds a place in this system. Still, every role matters. Remove any one of them, and the town would slowly stop working.",
    "articleZh": "每个城镇都需要有人来承担各种角色。在我住的街区，一位商业顾问就住在一家兽医诊所旁边，那里整天都在救治生病的动物。街对面，一位学校辅导员倾听着焦虑的青少年，一位英国事务律师起草法律文件，一位美国律师则为公司提供合同方面的建议。到了周六，那位沉默寡言的律师会变成棒球场上的裁判。超市的收银员记得每个人的名字，消防站里的消防员是当地的英雄，诊所的护士则常常值长夜班。我们的园丁负责修剪公园的草坪，理发师每个月给我剪一次便宜的头发。在港口边，一位渔夫把捕到的鱼卖给屠夫，而屠夫还养了两匹马，并雇了一个男孩给马梳毛。\n\n去年冬天，一名劫匪在银行里把一位顾客扣为人质。那位消防员冷静地和他谈了一个小时，直到警察赶到。事后他说自己并不算特别勇敢，他只是不想在自己孩子面前做个懦夫。\n\n这些工作很少光鲜。许多人为微薄的收入辛苦劳作，有些人觉得自己成了时间的奴隶。车站外面，一个乞丐向路人讨要零钱，提醒我们并非每个人都能在这个体系里找到位置。不过，每一个角色都很重要。少了其中任何一个，这个城镇都会慢慢停止运转。",
