    "id": "c20p1",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 1,
    "articleTitle": "Small Deeds in the Garden",
    "articleEn": "Every Saturday morning, Daniel goes to the community garden to {{act}} as a volunteer. At first he did not know how to {{behave}} there. One clumsy {{deed}}, knocking over a tray of seedlings, made his face turn red. The old gardener beside him did not {{glare}} at him; she only laughed and handed him a spade. Slowly he began to {{accustom}} himself to the work, and he learned to {{react}} calmly when something went wrong.\n\nNow he knows how to {{respond}} to the seasons. In spring he spreads compost to {{nourish}} the soil; in summer he must {{mow}} the long grass before it swallows the flowers. The volunteers {{support}} one another, sharing tools and advice, so even weak plants {{survive}} the cold months and {{revive}} in April.\n\nDaniel loves the small moments. He stops working, {{exhales}} slowly, and enjoys the deep {{intake}} of cool morning air. Sometimes he catches a {{glimpse}} of a fox near the hedge, or he sees children {{peep}} through the wooden fence, curious about the vegetables. He gives them a friendly {{glance}} and invites them in. When the sun goes down, he likes to {{gaze}} at the red sky above the rooftops.\n\nLater, on the bus home, he {{reflects}} on how much he has changed. He has decided to {{adopt}} one simple rule: do one useful thing for other people every day. Small actions, he believes, slowly build a better person.",
    "articleZh": "每个周六早上，丹尼尔都会去社区花园担任志愿者。起初，他不知道在那里该如何举止得体。一次笨手笨脚的行为——他打翻了一盘幼苗——让他的脸涨得通红。旁边那位年长的园丁并没有怒视他，只是笑了笑，递给他一把铁铲。渐渐地，他开始习惯这份工作，也学会了在出错时冷静地做出反应。\n\n现在他懂得如何顺应季节。春天他撒下堆肥来滋养土壤；夏天他必须在杂草吞没花朵之前把长草割掉。志愿者们互相支持，共享工具和经验，因此连虚弱的植物也能熬过寒冷的月份，并在四月复苏。\n\n丹尼尔喜爱这些细小的时刻。他停下手中的活，缓缓呼气，享受清凉晨风的深深吸入。有时他会瞥见树篱旁的一只狐狸，或者看到孩子们从木栅栏的缝隙里偷看，对这些蔬菜充满好奇。他友好地看他们一眼，邀请他们进来。太阳落下时，他喜欢凝视屋顶上方那片红色的天空。\n\n后来，在回家的公交车上，他会反思自己改变了多少。他决定采纳一条简单的准则：每天为别人做一件有用的事。他相信，小小的行动会慢慢造就一个更好的人。",
