    "id": "c20p2",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 2,
    "articleTitle": "A Decision at the Window",
    "articleEn": "Late one evening, Tom stood at the window and {{peer}}ed into the dark street. He did not want to simply {{stare}} at the traffic; he needed to {{contemplate}} a difficult choice.\n\nYears ago he had made a {{vow}} to his sister, Ana, and to him that promise was as serious as an {{oath}} in court: he would never work for the family shop. Last week, however, he had signed a {{pledge}} to manage it for one year.\n\nSomeone {{whistle}}d outside. It was Ana. When she asked what he had decided, he did not know how to {{reply}}.\n\n\"The bank rang to {{notify}} us about the loan,\" she said. Then she began to {{assert}} that he was the only person who could rescue the business. Tom tried to {{explain}} his fears, but within a minute they were beginning to {{quarrel}}.\n\nTheir {{dispute}} was an old one. Every {{argument}} followed the same pattern: Ana would {{mention}} their mother's illness, and Tom would fall silent.\n\n\"Please don't {{hurry}} me,\" he said. \"You always {{hasten}} decisions that need time.\"\n\nAna looked down. She did not {{urge}} him again, and she did not {{scold}} him like a child. \"I'm sorry I {{curse}}d at you last week,\" she said. \"I was frightened, that's all.\"\n\nTom nodded slowly. He watched the empty street for another minute, then made a quiet decision. This time, nobody had to push him.",
    "articleZh": "一天深夜，汤姆站在窗前，凝视着漆黑的街道。他并不想只是呆呆地看着车流；他需要认真思考一个艰难的选择。\n\n多年前，他曾对妹妹安娜许下承诺，在他看来，那个承诺就像法庭上的誓言一样严肃：他绝不会为家里的店铺工作。然而上周，他却签下了一份保证书，答应管理那家店一年。\n\n外面有人吹了声口哨。是安娜。当她问他决定得怎么样时，他不知道该怎么回答。\n\n\"银行打电话来通知我们贷款的事，\"她说。接着她开始断言，他是唯一能拯救这家生意的人。汤姆试着解释自己的担忧，但不到一分钟，他们就开始吵架。\n\n他们的争执是个老问题。每一次争论都是同样的套路：安娜会提起母亲的病，然后汤姆就沉默下来。\n\n\"请别催我，\"他说。\"你总是把需要时间的决定往前赶。\"\n\n安娜低下了头。她没有再劝他，也没有像对孩子那样责骂他。\"上周我对你骂了脏话，对不起，\"她说。\"我只是害怕。\"\n\n汤姆慢慢点了点头。他又看了一分钟空荡荡的街道，然后悄悄做出了决定。这一次，没有人需要推他一把。",
