    "id": "c20p3",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 3,
    "articleTitle": "Sports Day Manners",
    "articleEn": "Last spring, our coach turned sports day into a lesson about behaviour. He hated to {{preach}}, so he kept it short: \"Don't {{swear}} when you lose, and never {{provoke}} the other team.\"\n\nA few boys still liked to {{boast}} about how fast they were. They would {{tease}} the slower runners and even {{mock}} the way those students breathed. The coach asked them to think about how cruel words {{touch}} a person's heart. It took time, but they slowly began to {{grasp}} his point.\n\nIn the relay, I had to {{catch}} the baton from Lin. I was so nervous that I almost {{snatched}} it out of her hand. In the end I did {{grab}} it awkwardly, and my {{grip}} was far too tight. I made a {{mess}} of the first corner and had to {{twist}} my body to stay inside my lane. Somehow, on the last straight, I managed to {{overtake}} two runners.\n\nThe crowd started to {{clap}} before I even crossed the line, and my classmates stood up to {{applaud}}. I had to {{kneel}} on the grass to get my breath back. Lin came running over to {{hug}} me, laughing that she had never seen anyone run so badly and still win.\n\nLater, the coach said something I still remember: respect should {{follow}} you off the track. Winning feels good for one afternoon, but the way you treat people stays with you for years.",
    "articleZh": "去年春天，我们的教练把运动会变成了一堂关于行为举止的课。他不喜欢说教，所以只讲了一句话：\"输了不要骂人，也绝不要挑衅对手。\"\n\n还是有几个男生喜欢吹牛，炫耀自己跑得多快。他们会逗弄跑得慢的同学，甚至嘲笑那些人喘气的样子。教练让他们想一想，刻薄的话会怎样触动一个人的内心。这花了一些时间，但他们慢慢开始领会他的意思。\n\n接力赛中，我要从林那里接过接力棒。我太紧张了，差点从她手里把棒抢走。最后我还是笨拙地一把抓住了它，而且握得太紧了。第一个弯道我跑得一团糟，只好扭动身体才留在自己的跑道里。不知怎么，在最后的直道上，我竟然超过了两名选手。\n\n我还没冲过终点线，观众就开始拍手，同学们也站起来为我喝彩。我不得不跪在草地上喘气。林跑过来抱住我，笑着说她从没见过有人跑得这么难看还能赢。\n\n后来，教练说了一句我至今记得的话：尊重应当跟随你走下赛场。赢的感觉能让你高兴一个下午，但你对待别人的方式会陪伴你很多年。",
