    "id": "c20p4",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 4,
    "articleTitle": "Hands-On at the Workshop",
    "articleEn": "At the community workshop, we learn physics by doing small things with our hands. First, our teacher asks us to {{scatter}} a few dry beans across the table so we can count them. Then we {{fold}} a sheet of paper into a tiny box, {{fasten}} the lid with tape, and {{loosen}} it again to see how the folds hold. Nobody is allowed to {{smash}} anything, though one boy did {{scratch}} the desk with a screwdriver by accident. He had to {{wipe}} the mark with a cloth, {{scrape}} off the dried glue, and {{polish}} the wood until it shone.\n\nNext we {{split}} into pairs. Each pair gets a small motor. When we switch it on, the paper flags {{sway}} gently, the whole table seems to {{shake}}, and the metal plate begins to {{vibrate}} with a low buzz. Above it, a light card starts to {{whirl}} in the air, while the wheels {{rotate}} slowly and steadily. We also {{shuffle}} a pack of cards, drop two marbles down a slope and watch them {{collide}}; the moment they {{contact}} each other, both change direction.\n\nFinally, we {{connect}} the wires to a battery and {{combine}} everything into one machine. It is noisy and far from perfect, but it works. Our teacher smiles and says that science is not only about reading books; it is also about what your hands can actually do.",
    "articleZh": "在社区工作室里，我们通过动手做一些小事情来学习物理。首先，老师让我们把几颗干豆子撒在桌面上，好让我们数一数。然后我们把一张纸折成一个小盒子，用胶带把盖子固定好，再把它松开，看看折痕是怎么支撑住的。谁都不许砸坏任何东西，不过有个男孩还是不小心用螺丝刀把桌子划伤了。他只好用布把痕迹擦掉，把干了的胶水刮下来，再把木头擦亮，直到它发出光泽。\n\n接下来我们分成两人一组。每组拿到一个小马达。我们把它打开时，纸做的小旗轻轻摆动，整张桌子好像都在晃动，金属板也开始震动，发出低低的嗡嗡声。在它上方，一张轻飘飘的卡片开始在空中旋转飞舞，而轮子则缓慢平稳地转动。我们还洗了一副牌，把两颗弹珠从斜坡上放下去，看着它们相撞；就在它们彼此接触的那一刻，两颗弹珠都改变了方向。\n\n最后，我们把电线连接到电池上，把所有部件组合成一台机器。它很吵，也远不算完美，但确实能运转。老师笑着说，科学不只是读书，也在于你的双手真正能做到什么。",
