    "id": "c20p5",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 5,
    "articleTitle": "The Locksmith's Gamble",
    "articleEn": "Marco wanted to {{integrate}} into the local community, so he opened a small workshop near the harbour. Curious neighbours would {{trail}} behind him as he worked, watching his hands {{manipulate}} tiny tools with surprising calm. He could {{insert}} a thin wire into any lock, {{tilt}} it slightly, and {{pierce}} the mechanism until it clicked open. Light seemed to {{penetrate}} even the oldest keyholes under his fingers.\n\nOne evening a fisherman asked him to {{tow}} a broken boat back to shore. Marco agreed to {{arrange}} the ropes and {{steer}} the vessel himself, though he had never sailed at night. Friends said it was foolish to {{bet}} his reputation on one favour, to {{stake}} everything on luck. \"You {{gamble}} too much,\" they warned. But he made a {{promise}}, and promises {{attract}} respect in small towns.\n\nThe sea did not {{obsess}} him, yet the black water {{mesmerize}}d him as the engine coughed. For a moment he imagined a {{nightmare}}: the rope snapping, the boat lost. Instead, the moon rose and the waves calmed. When he reached the pier at dawn, the villagers were waiting to {{amaze}} him with applause. Someone joked that they should {{baptize}} the rescued boat with a new name: Second Chance. Marco laughed, exhausted but proud. He had won something more valuable than money that night.",
    "articleZh": "马可想融入当地社区，于是在港口附近开了一家小工坊。好奇的邻居们常常跟在他身后，看着他的双手以惊人的镇定操控细小的工具。他能把一根细铁丝插进任何一把锁，稍微倾斜一下，再刺入内部机构，直到锁咔哒一声打开。在他的手指下，光线似乎连最古老的锁孔都能穿透。\n\n一天傍晚，一位渔民请他把一条坏了的船拖回岸边。马可同意亲自整理绳索并驾驶那条船，尽管他从未在夜间航行过。朋友们说，为了一个人情就拿自己的名声去打赌、把一切押在运气上，实在太傻了。\"你赌得太大了，\"他们警告道。但他做出了承诺，而承诺在小镇上是能赢得尊重的。\n\n大海并没有让他着迷到无法自拔，可当发动机咳嗽般作响时，那片漆黑的海水还是把他迷住了。有一瞬间，他想到了一个噩梦般的画面：绳子断裂，小船消失。然而，月亮升起来了，海浪也平静下来。当他在黎明时分靠上码头，村民们正等着用掌声让他惊叹不已。有人开玩笑说，应该给这条获救的船举行命名礼，取个新名字：第二次机会。马可笑了，疲惫却自豪。那一夜，他赢得了比金钱更宝贵的东西。",
