    "id": "c20p7",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 7,
    "articleTitle": "The Task Force",
    "articleEn": "Last spring the government {{designated}} a special police unit to fight organised crime, and my cousin was {{assigned}} to it. Her team studies gangs that {{kidnap}} business people for ransom, {{hijack}} lorries on quiet roads, and {{smuggle}} weapons across the border in boxes of fruit.\n\nThe gangs are clever. They {{disguise}} themselves as delivery drivers, and the {{allure}} of easy money helps them {{tempt}} poor young men into the group. Recruiters {{induce}} teenagers to join by offering cash, and they use a friendly older member as {{bait}}. Once inside, nobody can {{undo}} that decision or {{detach}} himself from the network.\n\nPolice work is slow because criminals {{impede}} every investigation: they destroy phones and pay witnesses to stay silent. Still, the unit {{distributes}} information to smaller stations, and officers are {{despatched}} the moment a threat appears. Twice this year they {{intervened}} before violence began. On one occasion a gang leader had already tried to {{strangle}} a witness with a rope.\n\nMy cousin says the hardest problem is history. Fifty years ago the same region suffered a {{massacre}}, and the {{decimation}} of whole villages left families with no trust in the law. Rebuilding that trust matters as much as courts that {{convict}} guilty men.",
    "articleZh": "去年春天，政府指定成立了一支打击有组织犯罪的特别警队，我的表姐被派到了那里。她的小组研究那些绑架商人索取赎金、在僻静公路上劫持卡车、并把武器藏在水果箱里走私过境的团伙。\n\n这些团伙很狡猾。他们把自己伪装成送货司机，而轻松赚钱的诱惑帮他们把贫穷的年轻人引诱进组织。招募者用现金诱使青少年加入，还会让一个friendly的年长成员充当诱饵。一旦进去，没有人能撤销那个决定，也无法让自己脱离这个网络。\n\n警方的工作进展缓慢，因为罪犯会阻碍每一次调查：他们毁掉手机，花钱让证人保持沉默。尽管如此，这支警队会把情报分发给各个小警局，一旦出现威胁，警员就会被派遣出去。今年他们有两次在暴力发生之前就进行了干预。其中一次，一名团伙头目已经试图用绳子勒死一名证人。\n\n我表姐说，最难的问题是历史。五十年前，同一地区发生过一场大屠杀，整个村庄被大量摧毁，使得许多家庭对法律毫无信任。重建这种信任，与法院能否定罪有罪之人同样重要。",
