    "id": "c20p8",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 8,
    "articleTitle": "Maya's First Project",
    "articleEn": "When Maya joined the community centre, she did not {{conceal}} her nervousness. She could have {{refused}} the position, but she believed the team should never {{exclude}} anyone who was willing to learn. Her manager, Mr Ali, hoped to {{reverse}} the centre's falling attendance, so he asked her to {{undertake}} a new project: a weekend club for teenagers.\n\nHe tried to {{assure}} her that the plan was simple. The contract did {{stipulate}} clear duties: plan activities, {{sort}} the donated books, and send a report every Monday. Still, Maya hesitated. To {{convince}} her, Mr Ali showed her the budget; to {{reassure}} her further, he promised extra help.\n\nMaya's {{wish}} had always been to work with young people. She {{aspired}} to become a teacher, and her {{desire}} to make a difference was strong. Many of the teenagers she met {{yearned}} for attention; some would {{invoke}} family problems to explain their anger. Whenever her fingers {{itched}} to write a resignation letter, she remembered why she had come.\n\nHer first {{attempt}} at a debate night failed, because only two students arrived. Instead of quitting, she continued to {{strive}}. Every {{effort}} counted: posters in the library, phone calls to parents, small prizes for the winners. Two months later, thirty noisy teenagers filled the room, and Maya finally {{fulfilled}} the promise she had made to Mr Ali.",
    "articleZh": "玛雅刚到社区中心时,并没有掩藏自己的紧张。她本可以拒绝这个职位,但她相信团队绝不应该排斥任何愿意学习的人。她的经理阿里先生希望扭转中心参与人数不断下降的局面,于是请她承担一个新项目:一个面向青少年的周末俱乐部。\n\n他试图向她保证,这个计划很简单。合同里确实明确规定了职责:策划活动、整理捐赠的图书,并且每周一提交报告。尽管如此,玛雅还是犹豫。为了说服她,阿里先生给她看了预算;为了进一步让她安心,他承诺提供额外的帮助。\n\n玛雅一直以来的愿望就是与年轻人一起工作。她渴望成为一名教师,想要带来改变的愿望非常强烈。她遇到的许多青少年都渴求关注;有些人会拿家里的问题来解释自己的愤怒。每当她手痒得想写辞职信时,她就会想起自己为什么来到这里。\n\n她第一次尝试举办辩论之夜失败了,因为只来了两个学生。她没有放弃,而是继续努力。每一份付出都算数:在图书馆贴海报、给家长打电话、为获胜者准备小奖品。两个月后,三十个吵闹的青少年挤满了房间,玛雅终于履行了她对阿里先生许下的承诺。",
