    "id": "c20p9",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 9,
    "articleTitle": "Actions by the Old River",
    "articleEn": "As the deadline {{loom}}ed, our class decided to {{launch}} a small clean-up project by the old river. We {{commence}}d with research: for years, factories had {{exploit}}ed the water and left it grey and lifeless. Before doing anything, we went out to {{explore}} the banks and record what we saw.\n\nThen the real work began. We had to {{exert}} a lot of energy simply to {{clear}} a path through the weeds, and no small group could {{tackle}} the rubbish alone, so fifty volunteers joined us. They {{cope}}d with rain, mud and mosquitoes without complaining. Everything we collected was sorted and {{dispose}}d of properly, and afterwards we {{conduct}}ed a short survey among local residents.\n\nWriting the report was the hard part. I {{omit}}ted two key figures by mistake, and then {{delete}}d the wrong document while trying to correct it. For an hour I was afraid we would have to {{cancel}} the presentation. Fortunately, the damp weather had not {{erase}}d the handwritten labels on our folders, so a friend managed to {{rescue}} the original numbers from them. We never had to {{resort}} to guessing.\n\nIn two days we {{recover}}ed the lost data, {{restore}}d the file, and {{rectify}}ed every error in the tables. Standing by the clean water, I realised that useful action is rarely dramatic. It is mostly patient repair: you notice a problem, you face it, and you fix what you can.",
    "articleZh": "随着截止日期逼近,我们班决定在老河边启动一个小型清理项目。我们从调研开始:多年来,工厂一直在开发利用这条河的河水,把它弄得灰暗而毫无生机。在动手之前,我们先去实地考察河岸,记录看到的情况。\n\n接着真正的工作开始了。我们必须使出很大力气,才能在杂草中清出一条小路;而仅靠一个小团队无法独自应对这么多垃圾,于是有五十名志愿者加入了我们。他们默默地对付着雨水、泥浆和蚊子,没有一句抱怨。我们收集到的所有东西都经过分类并妥善处理,之后我们还在当地居民中开展了一次简短的问卷调查。\n\n写报告才是最难的部分。我不小心遗漏了两个关键数据,又在试图更正时删掉了错误的文件。有一个小时,我担心我们只能取消那次展示。幸好潮湿的天气并没有把文件夹上手写的标签抹掉,一位朋友因此成功从上面救回了原始数字。我们始终不必求助于猜测。\n\n两天之内,我们找回了丢失的数据,恢复了文件,并纠正了表格里的每一处错误。站在清澈的水边,我明白了:有用的行动很少是戏剧性的。它多半是耐心的修补——你发现问题,面对它,然后修好你力所能及的部分。",
