    "id": "c20p10",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 10,
    "articleTitle": "Redeeming an Old Warehouse",
    "articleEn": "Last spring our neighbourhood set out to {{redeem}} an old warehouse that had stood empty for years. Volunteers first had to {{obtain}} permission from the council, which {{offered}} a small grant to {{offset}} the cost of repairs. The money did not cover everything, so we held a book sale to {{raise}} extra funds, and two local shops agreed to {{supply}} paint and timber for free.\n\nThe work was simple but steady. Every Saturday we {{replenished}} our stock of nails and brushes, {{enlarged}} the reading room by taking down a wall, and {{augmented}} the weak lighting with second-hand lamps. A retired engineer {{rendered}} the floor safe by strengthening the beams, and he taught us to check the roof for any {{leak}} before the rainy season. We also installed a {{backup}} generator, because the electricity in that street often fails.\n\nSlowly the project began to {{gain}} support. Photographs on the noticeboard {{magnified}} every small step forward, and social media {{amplified}} our message. A few neighbours {{exaggerated}} how much we had achieved, but nobody minded, because the attention {{propelled}} us forward. We {{update}} the website every week and {{uphold}} one simple rule: whoever borrows a book must bring it back. To {{prolong}} the life of the project, we are now training younger volunteers, so the warehouse will still be open long after we stop.",
    "articleZh": "去年春天，我们社区决定改造一座空置多年的旧仓库。志愿者首先要从议会获得许可，而议会提供了一小笔补助，用来抵消维修的费用。这笔钱并不能覆盖全部开支，于是我们举办了一次旧书义卖来筹集额外资金，还有两家本地商店同意免费供应油漆和木材。\n\n这项工作简单却持续不断。每个星期六，我们都会补充钉子和刷子的存货，拆掉一面墙以扩大阅览室，并用二手台灯来增强昏暗的照明。一位退休工程师通过加固横梁使地板变得安全，他还教我们在雨季来临前检查屋顶有没有漏水的地方。我们也安装了一台备用发电机，因为那条街的电力经常中断。\n\n渐渐地，这个项目开始获得支持。公告板上的照片把每一点小小的进步都放大了，社交媒体则扩大了我们的声音。有几位邻居夸大了我们的成绩，但没有人在意，因为这些关注推动着我们前进。我们每周更新网站，并坚守一条简单的规则：借书的人必须把书还回来。为了延长这个项目的生命，我们现在正在培训更年轻的志愿者，这样即使我们不再参与，仓库也会长期开放下去。",
