    "id": "c20p11",
    "chapter": 20,
    "page": 11,
    "articleTitle": "The Leak at the Edge of Town",
    "articleEn": "Last spring, a rusty tank near our village began to {{spill}} oil. At first, only a thin stream {{seeped}} through a crack, but within hours a dark paste {{oozed}} across the grass. Officials told the nearest families to {{evacuate}} while workers dug a deep {{trench}} to stop the flow. Heavy rain, however, {{saturated}} the soil, and the mud could no longer {{contain}} the leak.\n\nThe company manager offered a long {{excuse}}, claiming the pipes were simply too old. A few neighbours were willing to {{forgive}} him, but most of us {{regarded}} his words as empty. He tried to {{flatter}} the mayor, whom local businesses almost {{worship}}, yet photographs of the black fields had already {{aroused}} public anger. Within a week, those images {{triggered}} protests in three towns.\n\nWhat was the real {{cause}}? Money. For the {{sake}} of a small profit, the firm had delayed repairs for years. Its main {{purpose}} was speed, and safety had never been a serious {{objective}}.\n\nInstead of arguing, volunteers began to {{seek}} practical solutions. They used simple pumps to {{retrieve}} the oil floating on the pond, spread straw to absorb the rest, and recorded every step for the court case. The clean-up took two months. Today the grass is growing again, but nobody in the village has forgotten how quickly one careless action can damage a place that people love.",
    "articleZh": "去年春天，我们村附近一个生锈的储罐开始漏油。起初只有一股细流从裂缝里渗出来，但几小时之内，一片黑色的黏稠物就慢慢淌过草地。官员让最近的几户人家撤离，工人则挖了一条深沟来阻止油的蔓延。然而大雨把土壤浸透了，泥土再也无法把泄漏的油困住。\n\n公司经理给出了一长串借口，声称管道实在太老了。少数邻居愿意原谅他，但我们大多数人都把他的话看作空话。他试图讨好市长——当地商家几乎把这位市长奉若神明——可是黑色田地的照片早已激起了公众的愤怒。一周之内，这些图片就引发了三个镇的抗议。\n\n真正的原因是什么？是钱。为了一点小小的利润，这家公司多年来一直拖延维修。它主要的目的是速度，安全从来都不是一个认真对待的目标。\n\n志愿者们没有争吵，而是开始寻求实际的解决办法。他们用简单的水泵把浮在池塘上的油回收上来，撒上稻草吸收剩下的部分，并把每一个步骤都记录下来，用于法庭诉讼。清理工作花了两个月。今天草又长起来了，但村里没有人忘记：一个疏忽的举动能多么迅速地毁掉人们所热爱的地方。",
