    "id": "c21p3",
    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 3,
    "articleTitle": "Know Your Body",
    "articleEn": "At the community health centre, Dr Lin teaches a class called “Know Your Body”. She always begins with the hands. “Press your {{thumb}} into the {{palm}} of your other hand,” she says. “Now stretch each {{finger}} wide, then close them into a soft {{fist}}.”\n\nNext, the students put both hands on the {{chest}} and breathe slowly. Air fills each {{lung}}, and the {{rib}}s rise like a gentle wave. Dr Lin explains that the heart has four {{chamber}}s, and that every {{organ}} works better when we breathe deeply.\n\nThen she moves down to the {{abdomen}}. She shows a simple drawing: the {{liver}} on the right, the {{stomach}} just above it, the long {{intestine}} folded underneath, and a {{kidney}} on each side of the spine, close to the {{waist}}. In women, the {{womb}} sits low in the body. She also points to the thyroid {{gland}} in the neck, which helps control energy and mood.\n\nFinally, the class stands up. Dr Lin asks them to bend one {{knee}}, feel the long muscles in the {{thigh}}, and turn every {{joint}} slowly — ankles, hips and shoulders.\n\n“Health is not only about food and exercise,” she says. “It is also about attention. When you know how your body normally feels, you notice tension and stress much earlier, and then you can rest before you break down.”",
    "articleZh": "在社区健康中心，林医生开设了一门叫做“认识你的身体”的课。她总是从双手开始。“用你的拇指按压另一只手的手掌，”她说，“现在把每根手指都伸展开，然后轻轻握成拳头。”\n\n接着，学员们把双手放在胸部，缓慢地呼吸。空气充满每一片肺叶，肋骨像温柔的波浪一样起伏。林医生解释说，心脏有四个心室（腔），而当我们深呼吸时，每一个器官都会运作得更好。\n\n然后她把话题移到腹部。她展示了一张简单的图：右边是肝脏，胃就在它的上方，长长的肠子折叠在下面，脊柱两侧各有一个肾脏，靠近腰部。在女性体内，子宫位于身体较低的位置。她还指出颈部的甲状腺，它有助于调节精力和情绪。\n\n最后，全班站起来。林医生让他们弯曲一条腿的膝盖，感受大腿上长长的肌肉，并慢慢转动每一个关节——脚踝、髋部和肩膀。\n\n“健康不只关乎饮食和运动，”她说，“它也关乎关注。当你了解自己的身体平时是什么感觉时，你就能更早地察觉紧张和压力，然后在崩溃之前好好休息。”",
