    "id": "c21p4",
    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 4,
    "articleTitle": "Small Habits, Healthy Body",
    "articleEn": "Every morning I run one {{lap}} of the park before breakfast. At first my {{ankle}} felt stiff, and my {{heel}} hit the ground too hard, so I learned to land softly and push off with my {{toe}}. After ten minutes every {{muscle}} in my legs feels warm, each {{pore}} in my skin opens, and my {{pulse}} rises to a steady beat. Doctors say that gentle exercise keeps every {{artery}} clear and calms the {{nerves}} that carry stress signals to the brain. It also changes the balance of {{hormones}} in the body, which makes the {{immune}} system stronger.\n\nMorning sunlight is a powerful {{stimulus}} for the body clock. It resets my {{biorhythm}}, so I fall asleep earlier and wake up without an alarm. Small changes like this have improved my whole {{lifestyle}}, and the most useful {{habit}} is also the simplest: no screens after nine o'clock.\n\nI try to protect my {{sight}} as well. Long hours of close work damaged my {{eyesight}} last year, so now, every twenty minutes, I look at a distant {{view}} through the window. Green trees let my eyes relax, and this kind of {{visual}} break really works.\n\nIt makes {{sense}} to me that good health is not one big decision. It is hundreds of tiny ones, repeated quietly, day after day.",
    "articleZh": "每天早上，我都会在早餐前绕公园跑一圈。起初我的脚踝很僵硬，脚跟落地也太重，于是我学会了轻轻落地，再用脚趾发力蹬出去。十分钟后，我腿上的每一块肌肉都感觉暖了起来，皮肤上的每个毛孔都张开了，脉搏也升到一个平稳的节奏。医生说，温和的运动能让每一条动脉保持通畅，也能安抚那些把压力信号传到大脑的神经。它还会改变体内荷尔蒙的平衡，从而让免疫系统变得更强。\n\n清晨的阳光对生物钟来说是一种强有力的刺激。它重置了我的生理节律，所以我入睡更早，而且不用闹钟就能醒来。这样的小改变改善了我整个生活方式，而最有用的习惯也是最简单的一个：九点以后不看屏幕。\n\n我也努力保护自己的视力。去年长时间的近距离工作损害了我的目力，所以现在我每二十分钟就透过窗户看看远处的景色。绿色的树木让我的眼睛得以放松，这种视觉上的休息真的有效。\n\n在我看来这很合理：良好的健康并不是一个重大的决定，而是成百上千个微小的决定，日复一日地安静重复。",
