    "id": "c21p9",
    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 9,
    "articleTitle": "Body and Mind",
    "articleEn": "Last winter my uncle was {{suffering}} from constant back pain, and he would often {{lament}} that his active years were over. My aunt finally drove him to the {{hospital}} in town, where a friendly {{physician}} examined him and ordered several tests. Because our country has free {{healthcare}}, the visit cost him nothing. The building was clean and {{sanitary}}, and the staff explained every {{medical}} step in simple language.\n\nThe {{treatment}} plan had two parts. First, a {{surgeon}} performed a small {{operation}} on a damaged disc. It was not a major procedure like a {{transplant}}, but my uncle was still nervous, especially about the {{injection}} of anaesthetic before the surgery. Second, he attended physical {{therapy}} three times a week at a local {{clinic}}, where a trainer designed gentle exercises to rebuild his {{fitness}}.\n\nThe doctor also wrote a {{prescription}} for mild painkillers and reminded him that no pill is truly {{curative}} on its own. Good sleep, careful {{hygiene}}, a balanced diet and daily walking would do more to {{heal}} his body than medicine alone.\n\nSix months later, the pain is almost gone. My uncle admits that time and patience can {{cure}} what he thought was permanent. He now says the hardest part of recovery was not physical at all; it was learning to stay hopeful while his body slowly repaired itself.",
    "articleZh": "去年冬天，我叔叔一直饱受背痛的折磨，他常常哀叹自己活力充沛的岁月已经结束了。我婶婶最终开车把他送到镇上的医院，一位和蔼的内科医生为他做了检查，并安排了几项化验。因为我们国家有免费的医疗保健，这次就诊他没有花一分钱。那座楼房干净卫生，工作人员用简单的语言解释了每一个医疗步骤。\n\n治疗方案分为两部分。首先，一位外科医生对受损的椎间盘做了一个小手术。这并不像器官移植那样是大手术，但我叔叔还是很紧张，尤其是害怕手术前的麻醉注射。其次，他每周三次去当地一家诊所做物理治疗，那里的教练为他设计了温和的锻炼，以重建他的体能。\n\n医生还开了一张温和止痛药的处方，并提醒他，任何药片本身都不是真正有疗效的。良好的睡眠、注意个人卫生、均衡的饮食和每天散步，比单靠药物更能治愈他的身体。\n\n六个月后，疼痛几乎消失了。我叔叔承认，时间和耐心能够治好他原以为无法改变的问题。他现在说，康复中最难的部分根本不是身体上的，而是在身体缓慢自我修复的过程中学会保持希望。",
