    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 12,
    "articleTitle": "A Hundred Small, Happy Habits",
    "articleEn": "Doctors often say that {{laughter}} is medicine we can take for free. When we share a joke with friends, our bodies relax, our breathing slows, and a quiet {{joy}} spreads through us. It does not take much to {{please}} the mind: a walk in the park, a warm meal, or a short phone call home.\n\nI used to think health meant only diet and exercise. Now I {{rejoice}} in smaller things. The first {{thrill}} of cold water on a summer morning. The {{cheer}} of neighbours calling my name. The simple {{pleasure}} of reading in bed. These moments are {{agreeable}} and cost nothing, yet they {{exhilarate}} me more than any expensive holiday.\n\nOf course, results matter too. My last check-up was {{satisfactory}}, and my doctor said a lower heart rate is {{desirable}} for someone my age. But she added something {{exciting}}: people who stay socially active recover faster. That is why I am {{keen}} to join a community running club. The members train with real {{zeal}}, though nobody is too competitive.\n\nOur city has become more {{lively}} since the new riverside path opened. It is a {{lovely}} place at sunset, and I am especially {{fond}} of the old bridge. I {{favor}} evening runs, when the light is soft. Sometimes a bird will {{startle}} me from the reeds, and I laugh at myself.\n\nGood health, I have learned, is not one {{amazing}} discovery. It is a hundred small, happy habits.",
    "articleZh": "医生常说，笑声是我们可以免费服用的良药。当我们和朋友分享一个笑话时，身体会放松，呼吸会变慢，一种安静的喜悦会在心里蔓延。让心情愉快其实并不需要太多：去公园散散步、吃一顿热饭，或者给家里打个短短的电话。\n\n我以前以为健康只跟饮食和运动有关。现在我为更小的事情感到欣喜：夏日清晨冷水带来的第一阵激动；邻居喊我名字时的那份欢快；躺在床上读书的简单乐趣。这些时刻令人惬意，而且不花一分钱，却比任何昂贵的假期都更让我振奋。\n\n当然，结果也很重要。我上次体检的结果是令人满意的，医生说对我这个年纪的人来说，心率低一些是可取的。但她还补充了一件让人兴奋的事：保持社交活跃的人恢复得更快。所以我很渴望加入一个社区跑步俱乐部。成员们训练时充满热忱，不过没有人过于争强好胜。\n\n自从新的滨河步道开放以后，我们的城市变得更有生气了。日落时那里是个可爱的地方，我尤其喜爱那座老桥。我偏爱在傍晚跑步，因为那时的光线很柔和。有时一只鸟会从芦苇丛中飞出，把我惊吓一下，然后我就笑自己胆小。\n\n我渐渐明白，良好的健康并不是某一个惊人的发现，而是一百个微小而快乐的习惯。",
