    "id": "c21p13",
    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 13,
    "articleTitle": "The Doctor Who Made Me Slow Down",
    "articleEn": "Last year my life became so {{hectic}} that I stopped sleeping and eating properly. One evening a colleague was completely {{frank}} with me. \"You look exhausted,\" she said. \"Please take your health {{seriously}}.\" I was not {{proud}} of my habits, so the next morning I visited a small community clinic.\n\nThe doctor was a {{humble}} woman in her sixties. She wore a {{modest}} grey coat and welcomed me with a {{friendly}} smile. Her voice was {{gentle}} and her manner was {{polite}}, but her advice was refreshingly {{direct}}: walk for thirty minutes a day, eat less sugar, and go to bed before eleven.\n\nShe was {{humorous}} as well. \"Good health is not {{mysterious}},\" she laughed. \"It is boring. That is why we ignore it.\" Her simple answer {{astounded}} me, because I had expected tests, machines and expensive pills.\n\nShe was {{generous}} with her time, giving me forty minutes for an {{earnest}} conversation about stress at work. I became {{curious}} about the mind as well as the body, and she took a {{liberal}} view of treatment: rest, hobbies, sunlight and friendship all count.\n\nBefore I left, she said something I still remember. Hiding your pain is not {{manly}} or strong; it is simply lonely. Asking for help is the {{daring}} choice, and {{honesty}} with yourself is where recovery begins.\n\nSix months later my life is still busy, but I sleep, I walk, and I finally feel well.",
    "articleZh": "去年，我的生活变得如此忙乱，以至于我连睡觉和吃饭都不正常了。一天傍晚，一位同事对我说了非常坦率的话。她说：\"你看起来累坏了。请认真对待你的健康。\"我对自己的生活习惯并不感到自豪，于是第二天早上我去了一家小小的社区诊所。\n\n那位医生是一位六十多岁、谦逊的女士。她穿着一件朴素的灰色外套，用友好的微笑欢迎我。她的声音温柔，举止礼貌，但她的建议直接得让人耳目一新：每天步行三十分钟，少吃糖，十一点前上床睡觉。\n\n她也很幽默。她笑着说：\"健康并不神秘，它很枯燥，所以人们才会忽视它。\"她这个简单的回答让我大为震惊，因为我原本以为会有各种检查、仪器和昂贵的药片。\n\n她很大方地付出时间，用了四十分钟和我诚挚地谈论工作压力。我开始对心理和身体一样感到好奇，而她对治疗持一种开明的看法：休息、爱好、阳光和友谊都同样重要。\n\n在我离开之前，她说了一句我至今记得的话：隐藏痛苦并不是有男子气概或者坚强的表现，那只会让人孤独。求助才是勇敢的选择，而对自己诚实是康复的起点。\n\n六个月后，我的生活依然忙碌，但我能睡了，会去散步了，也终于感觉自己健康了。",
