    "id": "c21p14",
    "chapter": 21,
    "page": 14,
    "articleTitle": "A Week by the Sea",
    "articleEn": "Last spring my doctor expressed real {{concern}} about my stress levels and suggested a quiet holiday. I was {{eager}} to leave the noisy city, so I booked a week in a small, {{picturesque}} fishing village.\n\nThe family who ran the guesthouse were wonderfully {{hospitable}}. They were {{considerate}} about my strange working hours, and left a {{thoughtful}} note on my desk each morning telling me the weather. When I admitted that I had been sleeping badly, the mother was {{sympathetic}} instead of dismissive, and always {{ready}} to make me hot milk.\n\nEach day I enjoyed the {{freedom}} of choosing my own path along the cliffs, where the sunsets were almost {{romantic}}. I was {{careful}} not to walk too far at first, but as my legs grew stronger, my {{confidence}} returned.\n\nOne evening I arrived an hour late for dinner and rushed to {{apologize}}. The family accepted my {{apology}} with a laugh and showed me great {{mercy}}: they had kept the fish soup warm. I came to {{admire}} their unhurried, generous way of life; their patience was {{remarkable}}.\n\nBy the end of the week I was sleeping a {{sound}} eight hours and eating properly again. I felt deeply {{grateful}}, and I tried to express my {{gratitude}} by helping with the washing-up. Good health, I learned, is not only about exercise. It also grows out of kindness, rest, and people who care.",
    "articleZh": "去年春天，我的医生对我的压力水平表示了真切的担忧，并建议我去度一个安静的假。我迫切地想离开喧闹的城市，于是在一个小小的、风景如画的渔村订了一周的住处。\n\n经营民宿的那家人非常热情好客。他们对我奇怪的作息时间很体谅，每天早上还会在我的书桌上留一张贴心的便条，告诉我当天的天气。当我承认自己一直睡不好时，那位母亲很有同情心，而不是不以为意，并且总是乐意给我热一杯牛奶。\n\n每天我都享受着沿悬崖自由选择路线的自在，那里的日落几乎带着浪漫的气息。起初我很小心，不让自己走得太远，但随着双腿变得更有力，我的自信也回来了。\n\n有一天晚上我迟到了一个小时才去吃晚饭，赶忙道歉。那家人笑着接受了我的道歉，还格外宽容地为我把鱼汤一直温着。我渐渐开始欣赏他们不慌不忙、慷慨大方的生活方式；他们的耐心令人赞叹。\n\n到那一周结束时，我每晚能睡上香甜安稳的八个小时，也重新好好吃饭了。我心里充满感激，并试着通过帮忙洗碗来表达我的谢意。我明白了，健康不只关乎运动，它也源于善意、休息，以及那些真心关怀你的人。",
